# Prefer stdlib

Before writing parsing, encoding, or character-class helpers, check Zig 0.16 std (`zig0.16 env` → `std_dir`). Use std when it covers the need.

## Prefer

| Need | Use |
|------|-----|
| JSON | `std.json.parseFromSlice` / `Value` |
| Percent-encoding | `std.Uri.Component.percentEncode`, `std.Uri.percentDecodeInPlace` |
| ASCII letter/digit/hex | `std.ascii.isAlphanumeric`, `isAlphabetic`, `isDigit`, `isHex`, … |
| Base64 | `std.base64` |
| Hex of bytes | `std.fmt.bytesToHex` |

## Thin wrappers are fine

Project helpers (e.g. `util.urlEncode`) may wrap std for allocator/arena ergonomics or a fixed character set. Do not reimplement the algorithm underneath.

## When custom is OK

Protocol codecs with no std equivalent (e.g. LDAP BER), domain rules that are not general libraries, and HTML escaping remain fine as local code.

```zig
// BAD
const ok = (c >= 'A' and c <= 'Z') or (c >= 'a' and c <= 'z') or (c >= '0' and c <= '9');

// GOOD
const ok = std.ascii.isAlphanumeric(c) or c == '_';
```
